  file isn't committed, and [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/[39m is gitignored in this repo.

  [1mMain decision: build the page from the [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m components.[0m The new page uses [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m + [38;5;153mselectField[39m,
  [38;5;153mdataTable[39m, [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m and [38;5;153memptyState[39m, the same way [38;5;153moverview.js[39m does. It does not copy [38;5;153mservices.js[39m, which builds its
  HTML by hand with its own [38;5;153m.pill[39m classes and [38;5;153mescapeHtml[39m. The components already handle most of the spec:
  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m keeps the sort in hidden inputs.
  - [38;5;153mdataTable[39m sorts, builds the [38;5;153m?sort=&dir=[39m header links with [38;5;153maria-sort[39m, and shows replacement content when there are no
    rows.
  - The chip colors [38;5;153mok[39m/[38;5;153mbad[39m/[38;5;153mwarn[39m/[38;5;153minfo[39m match the spec's green/red/amber/blue.

  That means no edits to [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m or [38;5;153mapp.css[39m.

